 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Committed revisions are pushed to browsers over self-hosted WebSockets rather than five-second HTTPS polling or a hosted realtime service. This provides fast updates without recurring realtime vendor fees or provider coupling, in exchange for owning WebSocket connection capacity, session management, and reconnect/catch-up logic in-house. See [Change Delivery Mechanism](decisions/change-delivery.md).
